From: OpenWrt MT6990 integration
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: mtk-lynxi: keep MT6990 SDK force mode at link up

MT6990 config uses the SDK force-2.5G sequence, but the generic LynxI
pcs_link_up callback still runs afterwards.  Keep MT6990 isolated from that
generic force-mode tail and reproduce the SDK's final 0x31120009 mode write.

--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
@@ -411,6 +411,14 @@ static void mtk_pcs_lynxi_link_up(struct
 	struct mtk_pcs_lynxi *mpcs = pcs_to_mtk_pcs_lynxi(pcs);
 	unsigned int sgm_mode;
 
+	if (mpcs->flags & MTK_SGMII_FLAG_MT6990) {
+		/* SDK mtk_sgmii_setup_mode_force() leaves the 2.5G Gen2 PCS
+		 * in this exact force-mode contract at MAC link-up.
+		 */
+		regmap_write(mpcs->regmap, SGMSYS_SGMII_MODE, 0x31120009);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	/* In force mode the PCS provides no link status feedback,
 	 * so re-init the T-PHY here as the only chance to recover
 	 * from a bad analog calibration. In-band modes are handled
